       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily would be 16,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 4000 mg dose is also well above the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. That amount could cause serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and other toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale, and I'll add it to the order note."
