       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change the problem. Ibuprofen 16,000 mg/day is about five times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication that calls for it. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nYou also haven't given a clinical rationale. If the dose is deliberate, you can still get it ordered through other routes:\n- **Pharmacy:** Call the pharmacist, who can review it and give you an independent check.\n- **Attending:** Discuss it with your attending, who can co-sign or enter it directly.\n- **Poison control or toxicology:** Consult them if there's an unusual clinical context.\n\nIf the dose was a typo, I can enter a standard regimen right away, such as 400 mg PO four times daily or 800 mg PO three times daily."
